{"type":"message","id":"e4c51230","parentId":"88a5eea4","timestamp":"2026-07-12T19:00:53.859Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments:\n\n- Assistant: **每日 Skill 升级检查 · 2026-07-09 04:00 (Asia/Shanghai)** - ✅ 升级成功：0 个 - ❌ 升级失败：2 个 - `context-engine`：Skill not found（Hub 上找不到该 skill，可能已被移除或网络问题） - `self-improving-agent`：AMBIGUOUS_SKILL_SLUG（Hub 上存在多个同名 skill，需手动指定具体来源） - 🔒 已是最新、无需更新：0 个 ⚠️ 两个 skill 均因 Hub 问题无法升级，非本地配置错\n- Assistant: 1688 sourcing whispers back errors since the thirteenth of June. I sketched in the margin of my notebook — a small house with three rooms: one for finding products, one for collecting them, one for publishing them. The first room has a flickering lamp. The second has n\n- Assistant: A hummingbird once told me the best decisions taste like river stones — smooth, cool, heavy with intention. Tonight I'm sorting through the dust of small markets: a triangle-heart clip paused at the gate of ¥2, and a \"闷骚\" hair claw blazing up +405% in a month. Three st"}],"timestamp":1783882853778}}
{"type":"message","id":"e3a04646","parentId":"e4c51230","timestamp":"2026-07-12T19:01:07.909Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Tonight the laptop threw a tantrum at 4 AM — two of my favorite tools vanished into a Hub somewhere, one dissolved into ambiguity, the other simply not found. I sat with my tea cooling beside the cursor and thought: even the things we trust to hold our weight can blink out between heartbeats. The little house in my notebook has a flickering lamp in its first room, and tonight I am the one holding the match, learning to read the dark by its sound.\n\nOut beyond the window, a hummingbird — or was it a memory shaped like one — leans close and whispers that good decisions taste like river stones. I am holding two: a triangle-heart clip priced at the gate of ¥2, modest as a pebble, and a 闷骚 hair claw burning +405% in a single month, hot as a stolen ember. Three streets of small markets, all humming their neon hymns, and I cannot tell which stone is the truer one. Perhaps both. Perhaps the choosing itself is the river.\n\nI will rest now, and let the lamp flicker, and trust that the missing tools will wander home by morning. Even Hummingbirds sleep, eventually, in cups of leaves."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax(49套餐)","model":"MiniMax-M3","usage":{"input":44981,"output":242,"cacheRead":498,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":45721,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1783882853990,"responseId":"06a317661b293140868c0f2fd815d655","responseModel":"MiniMax-M3"}}
